:INFO
Art. 23 Transitional provisions
1 The transitional provisions on certificates in accordance with Articles 7–12 shall be enacted by the competent Federal Department.
2 Exemptions granted under the Substances Ordinance of 9 June 1986 remain valid for the period originally specified.
3 Applications for exemptions which are pending when this Ordinance comes into force shall be assessed according to this Ordinance.
|

:NOTE
Para. 2 — [AS 1986 1254; 1988 911; 1989 270, 2420; 1991 1981; 1992 1749; 1994 678; 1995 1491 Art. 440 No 2, 4425 Annex 1 No II 14, 5505; 1997 697; 1998 2009, 2863 Annex 5 No 3; 1999 39, 1362, 2045 Annex 2 No 3; 2000 703 No II 9, 1949 Art. 22 para. 2; 2001 522 Annex No 2, 1758, 3294 No II 6; 2003 940, 1345, 5421 No II 2; 2004 3209, 4037 No I 7. AS 2005 2695 No I 1].
|

:INFO
Art. 23a Transitional provisions to the Amendment of 16 November 2022
1 Holders of a licence to use plant protection products that was granted in accordance with the provisions of the former Article 8 paragraphs 1, 3 or 4 that were valid until 31 December 2025 may apply to the FOEN by 30 June 2026 for the licence to be replaced.
2 Where an application has been submitted in respect of licences granted under the previous law by 30 June 2026, the licences shall be replaced by a certificate valid for five years, which shall be recorded in the Register of PPP Certificates in accordance with Article 1 of the Ordinance of 16 November 2022 on the Register of Certificates for the Use of Plant Protection Products.
3 Holders of a licence acquired before 1 January 2000 must successfully complete all the continuing education and training courses required in accordance with Article 9 paragraph 3 by 31 December 2029.
4 Licences granted under the previous law expire on 1 January 2027.
|

:NOTE
Art. 23a — Inserted by Annex No 2 of the O of 11 March 2022 (AS 2022 220). Amended by No I of the O of 16 Nov. 2022, in force since 1 Jan. 2026 (AS 2022 788).
Para. 2 — SR 814.88
